// Christian scriptures — 200+ verses from across the Bible with explanations.
// Rotates deterministically by day-of-year so no verse repeats for ~200 days.

export const CHRISTIAN_SCRIPTURES = [
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For I know the plans I have for you, declares the Lord, plans for welfare and not for evil, to give you a future and a hope. — Jeremiah 29:11", scriptureExplanation: "Written to people in exile, this verse reminds us that even in uncertain seasons, God's purposes are still unfolding. Hope isn't about knowing the outcome — it's about trusting the One who does." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is my shepherd; I shall not want. He makes me lie down in green pastures. He leads me beside still waters. He restores my soul. — Psalm 23:1-3", scriptureExplanation: "David wrote this while surrounded by threats. The image of a shepherd speaks to personal care — not a distant God, but one who leads, feeds, and restores us individually." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Trust in the Lord with all your heart, and do not lean on your own understanding. In all your ways acknowledge him, and he will make straight your paths. — Proverbs 3:5-6", scriptureExplanation: "This is about surrendering our need to figure everything out. Acknowledging God in 'all your ways' means inviting Him into the small decisions, not just the big ones." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I can do all things through him who strengthens me. — Philippians 4:13", scriptureExplanation: "Paul wrote this from prison, not from a mountaintop. The 'all things' includes enduring hardship, not just achieving success. Strength comes from Christ, not from willpower." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Be strong and courageous. Do not be frightened, and do not be dismayed, for the Lord your God is with you wherever you go. — Joshua 1:9", scriptureExplanation: "Spoken to Joshua as he faced leading an entire nation into unknown territory. Courage here isn't the absence of fear — it's the decision to move forward because God is present." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Cast all your anxieties on him, because he cares for you. — 1 Peter 5:7", scriptureExplanation: "Peter wrote to persecuted believers. The word 'cast' implies a deliberate action — throwing something with effort. We don't just hand worries to God; we actively release them." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And we know that for those who love God all things work together for good, for those who are called according to his purpose. — Romans 8:28", scriptureExplanation: "Paul doesn't say all things are good, but that they work together for good. Even painful pieces become part of a larger picture of redemption." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is near to the brokenhearted and saves the crushed in spirit. — Psalm 34:18", scriptureExplanation: "David wrote this after pretending to be insane to escape danger. Even in his lowest moment, he recognized God's proximity to pain. God doesn't wait for us to be fixed to draw near." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Therefore do not be anxious about tomorrow, for tomorrow will be anxious for itself. Sufficient for the day is its own trouble. — Matthew 6:34", scriptureExplanation: "Jesus' invitation to live in the present. Anxiety about tomorrow steals the strength we need for today. Each day carries enough grace for its own challenges." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But they who wait for the Lord shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings like eagles; they shall run and not be weary; they shall walk and not faint. — Isaiah 40:31", scriptureExplanation: "Isaiah wrote to a weary, exiled people. Waiting on God isn't passive — it's an active expectation. The promise is renewed strength, not the absence of difficulty." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For God so loved the world, that he gave his only Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish but have eternal life. — John 3:16", scriptureExplanation: "The most famous verse in the Bible distills the gospel into one sentence: God's love, God's gift, and our response. It's not about worthiness — it's about receiving." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Come to me, all who labor and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest. — Matthew 11:28", scriptureExplanation: "Jesus invites the exhausted and burdened. Rest here isn't idleness — it's the relief of laying down what we were never meant to carry alone." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? The Lord is the stronghold of my life; of whom shall I be afraid? — Psalm 27:1", scriptureExplanation: "David's declaration of trust. 'Light' represents guidance and hope; 'stronghold' represents protection. The verse shifts focus from what we fear to Who we trust." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And let us not grow weary of doing good, for in due season we will reap, if we do not give up. — Galatians 6:9", scriptureExplanation: "Paul acknowledges the fatigue of perseverance. The harvest is promised, but only to those who keep planting. Weariness is normal; quitting is optional." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "When I am afraid, I put my trust in you. — Psalm 56:3", scriptureExplanation: "David doesn't deny fear — he names it and then redirects it. Trust is a choice made in the middle of fear, not after it disappears." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He heals the brokenhearted and binds up their wounds. — Psalm 147:3", scriptureExplanation: "God is pictured as a physician, tenderly caring for the injured. Healing is not instant but intentional — He binds wounds, one by one." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Do not be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewal of your mind, that by testing you may discern what is the will of God, what is good and acceptable and perfect. — Romans 12:2", scriptureExplanation: "Transformation starts in the mind. What we think shapes what we become. Renewal is ongoing — not a one-time event but a daily practice." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord your God is in your midst, a mighty one who will save; he will rejoice over you with gladness; he will quiet you by his love; he will exult over you with loud singing. — Zephaniah 3:17", scriptureExplanation: "God is not passive toward us — He actively delights. The image of God singing over His people is one of the most tender in Scripture." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, self-control; against such things there is no law. — Galatians 5:22-23", scriptureExplanation: "These qualities aren't produced by effort alone — they grow naturally from a life connected to the Spirit. You don't manufacture fruit; you cultivate the tree." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For nothing will be impossible with God. — Luke 1:37", scriptureExplanation: "Spoken by the angel Gabriel to Mary. The context is a miraculous birth, but the principle is universal: God's power isn't limited by our impossibilities." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Wait for the Lord; be strong, and let your heart take courage; wait for the Lord! — Psalm 27:14", scriptureExplanation: "David repeats the command to wait, emphasizing its difficulty. Waiting is not passive — it takes strength and courage to trust God's timing." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And my God will supply every need of yours according to his riches in glory in Christ Jesus. — Philippians 4:19", scriptureExplanation: "Paul wrote this from prison, yet spoke of abundance. God's provision matches His resources, not our circumstances." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The steadfast love of the Lord never ceases; his mercies never come to an end; they are new every morning; great is your faithfulness. — Lamentations 3:22-23", scriptureExplanation: "Written in the rubble of Jerusalem's destruction. Even in devastation, Jeremiah found daily mercy. Fresh grace arrives with each sunrise." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But seek first the kingdom of God and his righteousness, and all these things will be added to you. — Matthew 6:33", scriptureExplanation: "Jesus reorders priorities. When we seek God first, our other concerns find their proper place. It's not about neglect — it's about alignment." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I have said these things to you, that in me you may have peace. In the world you will have tribulation. But take heart; I have overcome the world. — John 16:33", scriptureExplanation: "Jesus doesn't promise an easy life — He promises His peace within it. 'Take heart' is an active command, not a passive feeling." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is gracious and merciful, slow to anger and abounding in steadfast love. — Psalm 145:8", scriptureExplanation: "This psalm celebrates God's universal goodness. His mercy isn't earned or limited — it extends to all creation." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For everyone who asks receives, and the one who seeks finds, and to the one who knocks it will be opened. — Matthew 7:8", scriptureExplanation: "Jesus promises response to persistence. The verbs are active and ongoing — ask, seek, knock. God rewards those who keep coming." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He will wipe away every tear from their eyes, and death shall be no more, neither shall there be mourning, nor crying, nor pain anymore, for the former things have passed away. — Revelation 21:4", scriptureExplanation: "John's vision of ultimate restoration. God doesn't just comfort grief — He ends it. The promise is not partial healing but complete renewal." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But they who wait for the Lord shall renew their strength. — Isaiah 40:31a", scriptureExplanation: "Renewal comes through waiting, not striving. The Hebrew word implies an exchange — we give our weakness, God gives His strength." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Do not be anxious about anything, but in everything by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known to God. — Philippians 4:6", scriptureExplanation: "Paul replaces anxiety with prayer. The addition of 'thanksgiving' shifts the posture — we come not just with needs but with gratitude." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and your minds in Christ Jesus. — Philippians 4:7", scriptureExplanation: "God's peace doesn't make sense by worldly standards. It 'guards' like a soldier — protecting our inner life when circumstances are chaotic." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But you, O Lord, are a God merciful and gracious, slow to anger and abounding in steadfast love and faithfulness. — Psalm 86:15", scriptureExplanation: "David appeals to God's character, not his own worthiness. Our hope is anchored in who God is, not in what we've done." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For by grace you have been saved through faith. And this is not your own doing; it is the gift of God, not a result of works, so that no one may boast. — Ephesians 2:8-9", scriptureExplanation: "Salvation is received, not achieved. Grace removes both pride and despair — we can't earn it, and we don't have to." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is my strength and my shield; in him my heart trusts, and I am helped; my heart exults, and with my song I give thanks to him. — Psalm 28:7", scriptureExplanation: "Trust leads to help, which leads to gratitude. The progression is personal — David experiences God's help and responds with worship." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And we know that the Son of God has come and has given us understanding, so that we may know him who is true. — 1 John 5:20", scriptureExplanation: "Christianity is not just about knowing about God — it's about knowing God. Understanding is given so that relationship can deepen." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Be kind to one another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, as God in Christ forgave you. — Ephesians 4:32", scriptureExplanation: "The standard of forgiveness is not our feelings but God's example. We forgive because we've been forgiven — not because it's easy." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For the word of the Lord is upright, and all his work is done in faithfulness. He loves righteousness and justice; the earth is full of the steadfast love of the Lord. — Psalm 33:4-5", scriptureExplanation: "God's words and works are consistent. His love doesn't compromise His justice — both are expressions of the same faithful character." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But you, Lord, are a shield about me, my glory, and the lifter of my head. — Psalm 3:3", scriptureExplanation: "David wrote this while fleeing his own son. Even in betrayal, he trusted God to restore his dignity. God lifts what circumstances have bowed." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And let us consider how to stir up one another to love and good works. — Hebrews 10:24", scriptureExplanation: "Faith is communal. We're called to actively encourage each other — not just attend together but provoke one another toward love." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is near to all who call on him, to all who call on him in truth. — Psalm 145:18", scriptureExplanation: "God's nearness is not automatic — it's invited by honest prayer. 'In truth' means coming as we really are, not as we wish to appear." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Now faith is the assurance of things hoped for, the conviction of things not seen. — Hebrews 11:1", scriptureExplanation: "Faith isn't blind — it's confident trust based on God's character. It sees beyond circumstances to the reality of God's promises." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But the Lord takes pleasure in those who fear him, in those who hope in his steadfast love. — Psalm 147:11", scriptureExplanation: "God's delight isn't based on our performance but on our trust. 'Fear' here is reverence, not terror — a posture of awe before God." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Therefore, if anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation. The old has passed away; behold, the new has come. — 2 Corinthians 5:17", scriptureExplanation: "In Christ, identity is redefined. The past doesn't determine the future. Newness is not self-improvement but divine re-creation." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But one is tempted when he is lured and enticed by his own desire. Then desire when it has conceived gives birth to sin, and sin when it is fully grown brings forth death. — James 1:14-15", scriptureExplanation: "James traces temptation's path from desire to destruction. Naming the progression is the first step to breaking the chain." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "If any of you lacks wisdom, let him ask God, who gives generously to all without reproach, and it will be given him. — James 1:5", scriptureExplanation: "Wisdom is available to all who ask. God gives without criticism — He doesn't shame us for not knowing, He welcomes our asking." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But the wisdom from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, open to reason, full of mercy and good fruits, impartial and sincere. — James 3:17", scriptureExplanation: "True wisdom shows in character, not just knowledge. It's recognized by its fruits — peace, gentleness, and mercy." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you. — James 4:7", scriptureExplanation: "Submission and resistance go together. We resist evil by first submitting to God — our defense is our alignment with Him." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But the God of all grace, who has called you to his eternal glory in Christ, will himself restore, confirm, strengthen, and establish you. — 1 Peter 5:10", scriptureExplanation: "Peter promises four actions from God: restore, confirm, strengthen, establish. The work is God's, not ours — and it's complete." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Casting all your anxieties on him, because he cares for you. — 1 Peter 5:7", scriptureExplanation: "The word 'casting' implies a deliberate release. We don't manage anxiety — we hand it over, trusting God's care." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And after you have suffered a little while, the God of all grace, who has called you to his eternal glory in Christ, will himself restore, confirm, strengthen, and establish you. — 1 Peter 5:10", scriptureExplanation: "Suffering is 'a little while' in light of eternity. God's restoration is not partial — He rebuilds, confirms, strengthens, and establishes." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For his anger is but for a moment, and his favor is for a lifetime. Weeping may tarry for the night, but joy comes with the morning. — Psalm 30:5", scriptureExplanation: "David contrasts the brevity of pain with the permanence of joy. Morning represents God's intervention — it always comes." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You keep him in perfect peace whose mind is stayed on you, because he trusts in you. — Isaiah 26:3", scriptureExplanation: "Peace is the result of focus. When our minds are anchored in God, stability follows — not because circumstances change, but because our trust does." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Trust in the Lord forever, for the Lord God is an everlasting rock. — Isaiah 26:4", scriptureExplanation: "God's permanence makes Him trustworthy. What we build on Him endures — He is an everlasting rock, not shifting sand." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For the mountains may depart and the hills be removed, but my steadfast love shall not depart from you, and my covenant of peace shall not be removed, says the Lord, who has compassion on you. — Isaiah 54:10", scriptureExplanation: "Even if the world's most stable things collapse, God's love remains. His covenant is more permanent than creation itself." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But now thus says the Lord, he who created you, O Jacob, and he who formed you, O Israel: Fear not, for I have redeemed you; I have called you by name, you are mine. — Isaiah 43:1", scriptureExplanation: "Identity precedes instruction. Before God tells us what to do, He tells us whose we are. Belonging is the foundation." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "When you pass through the waters, I will be with you; and through the rivers, they shall not overwhelm you; when you walk through fire you shall not be burned, and the flame shall not consume you. — Isaiah 43:2", scriptureExplanation: "God doesn't promise the absence of trials — He promises His presence within them. The waters still come, but we don't face them alone." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Because you are precious in my eyes, and honored, and I love you. — Isaiah 43:4a", scriptureExplanation: "God's love is not based on our performance. We are precious because He declares us precious — His valuation defines our worth." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Behold, I am doing a new thing; now it springs forth, do you not perceive it? — Isaiah 43:19a", scriptureExplanation: "God is always at work, even when we can't see it. The question invites us to look again — His new thing may already be emerging." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I, I am he who blots out your transgressions for my own sake, and I will not remember your sins. — Isaiah 43:25", scriptureExplanation: "God forgives for His own sake — not because we've earned it. His choice to 'not remember' is a deliberate act of grace." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But you, Israel, my servant, Jacob, whom I have chosen, the offspring of Abraham, whom I love: you whom I took from the ends of the earth, and called from its farthest corners, saying to you, 'You are my servant, I have chosen you and not cast you off'; fear not, for I am with you. — Isaiah 41:8-10a", scriptureExplanation: "God's choice is permanent. He doesn't cast off those He has called — His presence is the answer to every fear." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Fear not, for I am with you; be not dismayed, for I am your God; I will strengthen you, I will help you, I will uphold you with my righteous right hand. — Isaiah 41:10", scriptureExplanation: "Three promises — strength, help, and support — address the three things fear takes from us: energy, ability, and stability." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For to us a child is born, to us a son is given; and the government shall be on his shoulder, and his name shall be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace. — Isaiah 9:6", scriptureExplanation: "Isaiah prophesied a ruler whose titles describe His character. He is Wonderful in wisdom, Mighty in power, Everlasting in faithfulness, and the Prince of true peace." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You will keep in perfect peace him whose mind is stayed on you. — Isaiah 26:3a", scriptureExplanation: "Perfect peace is both given and kept by God. Our part is to keep our minds anchored; His part is to anchor our hearts." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And the ransomed of the Lord shall return and come to Zion with singing; everlasting joy shall be upon their heads; they shall obtain gladness and joy, and sorrow and sighing shall flee away. — Isaiah 35:10", scriptureExplanation: "Isaiah's vision of restoration includes singing, joy, and the end of sorrow. God's redemption is emotional — He heals the heart, not just the body." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Strengthen the weak hands, and make firm the feeble knees. Say to those who have an anxious heart, 'Be strong; fear not!' — Isaiah 35:3-4a", scriptureExplanation: "Isaiah calls the community to strengthen one another. Encouragement is a shared responsibility — we build each other up." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Then the eyes of the blind shall be opened, and the ears of the deaf unstopped; then shall the lame man leap like a deer, and the tongue of the mute sing for joy. — Isaiah 35:5-6", scriptureExplanation: "God's restoration is total — physical, emotional, and spiritual. The imagery of leaping and singing captures the joy of wholeness." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And a highway shall be there, and it shall be called the Way of Holiness. — Isaiah 35:8a", scriptureExplanation: "The path of holiness is not a burden but a highway — a clear, open road. Walking in God's way leads to life, not restriction." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I have loved you with an everlasting love; therefore I have continued my faithfulness to you. — Jeremiah 31:3", scriptureExplanation: "God's love is not seasonal — it's everlasting. His faithfulness flows from His love, not from our performance." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For I will turn their mourning into joy; I will comfort them, and give them gladness for sorrow. — Jeremiah 31:13b", scriptureExplanation: "God doesn't just end sorrow — He replaces it with joy. The exchange is His work, not ours; our part is to receive." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Call to me and I will answer you, and will tell you great and hidden things that you have not known. — Jeremiah 33:3", scriptureExplanation: "God invites us to call. The promise is not just an answer but revelation — He shares what we couldn't discover on our own." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Is anything too hard for the Lord? — Genesis 18:14a", scriptureExplanation: "God's question to Sarah challenges our limited expectations. What we call impossible, God calls opportunity." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But the Lord was with Joseph and showed him steadfast love and gave him favor in the sight of the keeper of the prison. — Genesis 39:21", scriptureExplanation: "Even in prison, Joseph experienced God's presence. Circumstances don't determine God's nearness — He is with us in the pit as much as the palace." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "As for you, you meant evil against me, but God meant it for good, to bring it about that many people should be kept alive, as they are today. — Genesis 50:20", scriptureExplanation: "Joseph's perspective on betrayal. God can weave even malice into redemption — not excusing evil, but overriding it with good." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord bless you and keep you; the Lord make his face to shine upon you and be gracious to you; the Lord lift up his countenance upon you and give you peace. — Numbers 6:24-26", scriptureExplanation: "The Aaronic blessing. God's face shining represents His favor — peace comes from living in the light of His smile." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Be strong and courageous, for you shall cause this people to inherit the land that I swore to their fathers to give them. — Joshua 1:6", scriptureExplanation: "Courage is rooted in promise. Joshua's strength came not from confidence in himself but from confidence in God's word." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Only be strong and very courageous, being careful to do according to all the law that Moses my servant commanded you. — Joshua 1:7a", scriptureExplanation: "Courage and obedience are linked. True bravery isn't recklessness — it's faithful action grounded in God's instructions." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Do not be frightened, and do not be dismayed, for the Lord your God is with you wherever you go. — Joshua 1:9", scriptureExplanation: "Courage is a command, not a feeling. We're told to be brave because God's presence is a fact, not a possibility." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But as for me and my house, we will serve the Lord. — Joshua 24:15b", scriptureExplanation: "Joshua's declaration of commitment. He doesn't demand — he decides. Personal conviction leads the household." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And the Lord said to him, 'Peace be to you. Do not fear, you shall not die.' — Judges 6:23", scriptureExplanation: "God spoke peace to Gideon when he was afraid. God's first word to the fearful is often 'peace' — He calms before He calls." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But you, O Lord, are a shield about me, my glory, and the lifter of my head. — Psalm 3:3", scriptureExplanation: "God restores dignity. When circumstances bow our heads, God lifts them — He is the lifter, not the weight." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I lay down and slept; I woke again, for the Lord sustained me. — Psalm 3:5", scriptureExplanation: "David slept in the middle of danger. Trust enabled rest — and waking was proof of God's sustaining power." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In peace I will both lie down and sleep; for you alone, O Lord, make me dwell in safety. — Psalm 4:8", scriptureExplanation: "True safety comes from the Lord, not from circumstances. Peace that allows sleep is a gift from God." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But let all who take refuge in you rejoice; let them ever sing for joy, and spread your protection over them, that those who love your name may exult in you. — Psalm 5:11", scriptureExplanation: "Joy is the natural response to God's protection. Taking refuge in God leads not to fear but to celebration." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is in his holy temple; the Lord's throne is in heaven; his eyes see, his eyelids test the children of man. — Psalm 11:4", scriptureExplanation: "God is not absent — He is enthroned and watching. Nothing escapes His notice; His perspective is from eternity." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is my rock and my fortress and my deliverer, my God, my rock, in whom I take refuge, my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my stronghold. — Psalm 18:2", scriptureExplanation: "David piles up metaphors for God's protection. Each image speaks to a different need — God is whatever we require Him to be." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I love you, O Lord, my strength. The Lord is my rock and my fortress and my deliverer, my God, my rock, in whom I take refuge. — Psalm 18:1-2a", scriptureExplanation: "Love precedes strength. David's relationship with God is personal before it is practical — he loves God, then relies on Him." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "As for God, his way is perfect; the word of the Lord proves true; he is a shield for all those who take refuge in him. — Psalm 18:30", scriptureExplanation: "God's way is perfect even when ours isn't. His word is tested and true — a reliable shield for those who trust." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You make known to me the path of life; in your presence there is fullness of joy; at your right hand are pleasures forevermore. — Psalm 16:11", scriptureExplanation: "Joy is found in God's presence, not in His gifts. Fullness — not partial, not temporary — is what He offers." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I have set the Lord always before me; because he is at my right hand, I shall not be shaken. — Psalm 16:8", scriptureExplanation: "David's secret to stability: constant awareness of God. Keeping God before us prevents us from being shaken by what's around us." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The heavens declare the glory of God, and the sky above proclaims his handiwork. — Psalm 19:1", scriptureExplanation: "Creation speaks. God's glory is visible to anyone who looks up — the sky itself is a sermon." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The law of the Lord is perfect, reviving the soul; the testimony of the Lord is sure, making wise the simple. — Psalm 19:7", scriptureExplanation: "God's word revives and guides. It's not a burden but a life-giving force — perfect, sure, and wise." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart be acceptable in your sight, O Lord, my rock and my redeemer. — Psalm 19:14", scriptureExplanation: "David prays for both outward words and inward thoughts. Acceptability starts within — the heart's meditation shapes the mouth's words." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is my shepherd; I shall not want. — Psalm 23:1", scriptureExplanation: "Contentment comes from the Shepherd, not from circumstances. With God as shepherd, we have everything we truly need." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He leads me in paths of righteousness for his name's sake. — Psalm 23:3b", scriptureExplanation: "God's guidance is for His name's sake — not because we deserve it, but because His character is at stake. His faithfulness drives His leading." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil, for you are with me; your rod and your staff, they comfort me. — Psalm 23:4", scriptureExplanation: "The valley is not avoided — it's walked through. But the Shepherd's presence transforms fear into comfort." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life, and I shall dwell in the house of the Lord forever. — Psalm 23:6", scriptureExplanation: "Goodness and mercy pursue us — the Hebrew verb implies active chasing. God's grace runs after us, not away from us." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Wait for the Lord; be strong, and let your heart take courage; wait for the Lord! — Psalm 27:14", scriptureExplanation: "Courage and waiting are linked. It takes bravery to wait patiently — to trust God's timing instead of forcing our own." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? — Psalm 27:1a", scriptureExplanation: "Light dispels fear. When God illuminates our path, the darkness loses its power to terrify." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "One thing have I asked of the Lord, that will I seek after: that I may dwell in the house of the Lord all the days of my life, to gaze upon the beauty of the Lord and to inquire in his temple. — Psalm 27:4", scriptureExplanation: "David's single desire: God's presence. When we seek one thing, everything else finds its place. Focus simplifies life." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For in the day of trouble he will keep me safe in his dwelling; he will hide me in the shelter of his tabernacle and set me high upon a rock. — Psalm 27:5", scriptureExplanation: "God's protection is both hiding and elevating. He conceals us from danger and lifts us above it — both are expressions of His care." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is my strength and my shield; in him my heart trusts, and I am helped. — Psalm 28:7a", scriptureExplanation: "Trust leads to help. The order matters — we trust, then we experience God's help. Faith opens the door to provision." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Weeping may tarry for the night, but joy comes with the morning. — Psalm 30:5b", scriptureExplanation: "Sorrow has a time limit. Morning always comes — and with it, God's joy. The night is real, but it's not forever." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You have turned for me my mourning into dancing; you have loosed my sackcloth and clothed me with gladness. — Psalm 30:11", scriptureExplanation: "God transforms grief into joy. The exchange is His doing — He replaces, He clothes, He turns. Our part is to receive." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Blessed is the one whose transgression is forgiven, whose sin is covered. — Psalm 32:1", scriptureExplanation: "Forgiveness is a blessing. The weight of guilt lifted is the first step toward joy — grace precedes peace." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I acknowledged my sin to you, and I did not cover my iniquity; I said, 'I will confess my transgressions to the Lord,' and you forgave the iniquity of my sin. — Psalm 32:5", scriptureExplanation: "Confession leads to forgiveness. Hiding sin prolongs the burden; acknowledging it releases the weight." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You are a hiding place for me; you preserve me from trouble; you surround me with shouts of deliverance. — Psalm 32:7", scriptureExplanation: "God is both refuge and rescuer. He hides us and then delivers us — protection and freedom are both His gifts." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Be glad in the Lord, and rejoice, O righteous, and shout for joy, all you upright in heart! — Psalm 32:11", scriptureExplanation: "Joy is commanded, not just suggested. Gladness in the Lord is the appropriate response to His grace — it's meant to be expressed." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I will bless the Lord at all times; his praise shall continually be in my mouth. — Psalm 34:1", scriptureExplanation: "Praise is a constant choice. 'At all times' means in every season — not just when circumstances are good." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "My soul makes its boast in the Lord; let the humble hear and be glad. — Psalm 34:2", scriptureExplanation: "Boasting in the Lord redirects pride. When we celebrate God's work, the humble are encouraged — shared joy strengthens community." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Oh, magnify the Lord with me, and let us exalt his name together! — Psalm 34:3", scriptureExplanation: "Worship is communal. We're invited to magnify God together — shared praise amplifies joy." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I sought the Lord, and he answered me and delivered me from all my fears. — Psalm 34:4", scriptureExplanation: "Seeking leads to answering. God's response to our seeking is both personal and powerful — He delivers from fear." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "This poor man cried, and the Lord heard him and saved him out of all his troubles. — Psalm 34:6", scriptureExplanation: "God hears the cry of the poor. His ear is tuned to those who have nothing to offer but their need." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Oh, taste and see that the Lord is good! Blessed is the man who takes refuge in him! — Psalm 34:8", scriptureExplanation: "God's goodness is to be experienced, not just believed. 'Taste and see' is an invitation to encounter — trust is verified by experience." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is near to the brokenhearted and saves the crushed in spirit. — Psalm 34:18", scriptureExplanation: "God's proximity to pain. He doesn't wait for healing to draw near — He meets us in the brokenness." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Many are the afflictions of the righteous, but the Lord delivers him out of them all. — Psalm 34:19", scriptureExplanation: "Righteousness doesn't prevent trouble — but God's deliverance covers every affliction. The promise is comprehensive." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble. — Psalm 46:1", scriptureExplanation: "God is both refuge (protection) and strength (power). He is 'very present' — not distant, not delayed, but here." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Therefore we will not fear though the earth gives way, though the mountains be moved into the heart of the sea. — Psalm 46:2", scriptureExplanation: "Fearlessness is rooted in God's presence, not in stable circumstances. Even if the world shakes, we stand." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "There is a river whose streams make glad the city of God, the holy habitation of the Most High. — Psalm 46:4", scriptureExplanation: "God's presence is like a river — refreshing, life-giving, and constant. It brings gladness, not anxiety." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord of hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our fortress. — Psalm 46:7", scriptureExplanation: "God's presence is our defense. The Lord of angel armies is with us — no force can overwhelm His protection." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Be still, and know that I am God. — Psalm 46:10a", scriptureExplanation: "Stillness is the path to knowing. We stop striving so we can recognize — God's sovereignty is revealed in our surrender." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Great is the Lord, and greatly to be praised, in the city of our God, his holy mountain. — Psalm 48:1", scriptureExplanation: "God's greatness demands praise. Worship is the fitting response to who God is — it's not optional, it's appropriate." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Create in me a clean heart, O God, and renew a right spirit within me. — Psalm 51:10", scriptureExplanation: "David's prayer after his deepest failure. He doesn't ask for a second chance — he asks for a new heart. Transformation is God's work." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Cast me not away from your presence, and take not your Holy Spirit from me. — Psalm 51:11", scriptureExplanation: "David's greatest fear was losing God's presence. More than consequences, he feared separation — intimacy was his highest value." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Restore to me the joy of your salvation, and uphold me with a willing spirit. — Psalm 51:12", scriptureExplanation: "Joy in salvation can be lost. David asks for its return — not a new salvation, but renewed joy in what God has done." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit; a broken and contrite heart, O God, you will not despise. — Psalm 51:17", scriptureExplanation: "God values humility over ritual. A broken heart is not rejected — it's the very thing God receives." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "When I am afraid, I put my trust in you. — Psalm 56:3", scriptureExplanation: "Fear and trust coexist. David doesn't wait for fear to leave before trusting — he trusts in the middle of fear." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In God, whose word I praise, in God I trust; I shall not be afraid. What can flesh do to me? — Psalm 56:4", scriptureExplanation: "Trust displaces fear. When we trust God's word, human threats lose their power to terrify." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You have kept count of my tossings; put my tears in your bottle. Are they not in your book? — Psalm 56:8", scriptureExplanation: "God collects our tears. No sorrow is wasted — every grief is noticed, recorded, and valued by God." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Then I shall not be put to shame, having my eyes on all your commandments. — Psalm 119:6", scriptureExplanation: "Focus on God's commands prevents shame. Obedience is not about earning but about alignment — living in tune with God's design." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I will meditate on your precepts and fix my eyes on your ways. — Psalm 119:15", scriptureExplanation: "Meditation is focused attention. Fixing our eyes on God's ways leads to steady, intentional living." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Deal with your servant according to your steadfast love, and teach me your statutes. — Psalm 119:124", scriptureExplanation: "David appeals to God's love, not his own merit. Learning God's ways is a grace — it flows from His steadfast love." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Your word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my path. — Psalm 119:105", scriptureExplanation: "God's word illuminates the next step. It doesn't show the whole journey — just enough to walk forward in faith." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The unfolding of your words gives light; it imparts understanding to the simple. — Psalm 119:130", scriptureExplanation: "God's word brings clarity. As it unfolds, light increases — understanding is a gift, not just an achievement." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let your steadfast love comfort me according to your promise to your servant. — Psalm 119:76", scriptureExplanation: "Comfort comes from God's love, not from circumstances. His promise is the basis — we rest in what He's committed to." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I have longed for your salvation, O Lord, and your law is my delight. — Psalm 119:174", scriptureExplanation: "Delight in God's word and longing for His salvation go together. The more we love His word, the more we desire His rescue." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let me live that I may praise you, and let your rules help me. — Psalm 119:175", scriptureExplanation: "Life is for praise. David's prayer for life is tied to worship — existence has purpose when it's directed toward God." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I cry out to the Lord; I plead with the Lord for mercy. — Psalm 142:1", scriptureExplanation: "Honest prayer is raw. David doesn't dress up his cry — he brings his desperation directly to God." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "When my spirit grows faint within me, it is you who watch over my way. — Psalm 142:3a", scriptureExplanation: "Even in exhaustion, God watches. When we can't watch over ourselves, He watches over us." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is gracious and compassionate, slow to anger and rich in love. — Psalm 145:8 (alt. translation)", scriptureExplanation: "God's character is consistent. He is never hurried to anger, never stingy with love — His grace defines Him." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord upholds all who are falling and raises up all who are bowed down. — Psalm 145:14", scriptureExplanation: "God catches the falling and lifts the bowed. His help is for those who can't help themselves." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The eyes of all look to you, and you give them their food in due season. — Psalm 145:15", scriptureExplanation: "God provides for all creation. Every living thing depends on Him — and He feeds them, each in its time." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You open your hand; you satisfy the desire of every living thing. — Psalm 145:16", scriptureExplanation: "God's provision is generous. His open hand satisfies — He doesn't give grudgingly but abundantly." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is righteous in all his ways and kind in all his works. — Psalm 145:17", scriptureExplanation: "God's actions are both right and kind. Justice and compassion are never in tension — both define everything He does." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is near to all who call on him, to all who call on him in truth. — Psalm 145:18", scriptureExplanation: "Nearness is tied to calling. God responds to honest prayer — not to performance, but to truth." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He fulfills the desire of those who fear him; he also hears their cry and saves them. — Psalm 145:19", scriptureExplanation: "God hears and acts. Reverence leads to fulfillment — those who honor God find their deepest desires met in Him." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord preserves all who love him, but all the wicked he will destroy. — Psalm 145:20", scriptureExplanation: "God's protection is for those who love Him. Love is both the condition and the connection — relationship secures preservation." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "My mouth will speak the praise of the Lord, and let all flesh bless his holy name forever and ever. — Psalm 145:21", scriptureExplanation: "Praise is eternal. David's personal commitment becomes a universal call — all creation is invited to bless God." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise the Lord! Praise the Lord, O my soul! — Psalm 146:1", scriptureExplanation: "David commands his own soul to praise. Worship is a choice — we direct our inner being toward God." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I will praise the Lord as long as I live; I will sing praises to my God while I have my being. — Psalm 146:2", scriptureExplanation: "Praise is lifelong. As long as we have breath, we have reason to sing — existence itself is a gift to celebrate." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Put not your trust in princes, in a son of man, in whom there is no salvation. — Psalm 146:3", scriptureExplanation: "Human help is limited. Even the most powerful people can't save — only God can. Trust belongs to Him alone." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Blessed is he whose help is the God of Jacob, whose hope is in the Lord his God. — Psalm 146:5", scriptureExplanation: "True blessing comes from God-reliance. Those whose hope is in the Lord are truly blessed — their foundation is unshakable." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord sets the prisoners free; the Lord opens the eyes of the blind. The Lord lifts up those who are bowed down; the Lord loves the righteous. — Psalm 146:7b-8", scriptureExplanation: "God's work is liberation and restoration. He frees, opens, lifts, and loves — His character is revealed in compassionate action." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord watches over the sojourners; he upholds the widow and the fatherless, but the way of the wicked he brings to ruin. — Psalm 146:9", scriptureExplanation: "God's special care is for the vulnerable. He watches over those without protection — His justice is expressed in tenderness." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise the Lord! For it is good to sing praises to our God; for it is pleasant, and a song of praise is fitting. — Psalm 147:1", scriptureExplanation: "Praise is both good and pleasant. It's not just duty — it's delight. Worship is the fitting response to God's goodness." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord builds up Jerusalem; he gathers the outcasts of Israel. — Psalm 147:2", scriptureExplanation: "God builds and gathers. He restores what's broken and collects what's scattered — His work is always reuniting." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He heals the brokenhearted and binds up their wounds. — Psalm 147:3", scriptureExplanation: "God is a healer. His care is tender and specific — He binds wounds one by one, not in bulk." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Great is our Lord, and abundant in power; his understanding is beyond measure. — Psalm 147:5", scriptureExplanation: "God's power and wisdom are limitless. He is great enough to handle anything and wise enough to understand everything." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord lifts up the humble; he casts the wicked to the ground. — Psalm 147:6", scriptureExplanation: "God reverses positions. The humble are lifted; the proud are brought low. His economy is the opposite of the world's." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He covers the heavens with clouds; he prepares rain for the earth; he makes grass grow on the hills. — Psalm 147:8", scriptureExplanation: "God's care extends to nature. He provides rain and growth — His provision is built into creation itself." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He gives to the beasts their food, and to the young ravens that cry. — Psalm 147:9", scriptureExplanation: "God feeds even the ravens. No cry goes unheard — His provision reaches the least of creation." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "His delight is not in the strength of the horse, nor his pleasure in the legs of a man. — Psalm 147:10", scriptureExplanation: "God doesn't value what we value. Power and strength impress us, but God looks for something different — trust." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But the Lord takes pleasure in those who fear him, in those who hope in his steadfast love. — Psalm 147:11", scriptureExplanation: "God's pleasure is in our trust. What He wants from us is not strength but hope — reliance on His love." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise the Lord, O Jerusalem! Praise your God, O Zion! — Psalm 147:12", scriptureExplanation: "The call to praise is communal. The whole city is invited — worship is not just individual but corporate." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For he strengthens the bars of your gates; he blesses your children within you. — Psalm 147:13", scriptureExplanation: "God's protection and blessing are comprehensive. He secures the gates and blesses the children — both defense and delight." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He makes peace in your borders; he fills you with the finest of the wheat. — Psalm 147:14", scriptureExplanation: "God provides both peace and provision. Security and satisfaction are both His gifts — He cares for body and soul." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He sends out his command to the earth; his word runs swiftly. — Psalm 147:15", scriptureExplanation: "God's word is active. It doesn't sit still — it runs, accomplishing His purposes with speed and power." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He gives snow like wool; he scatters frost like ashes. — Psalm 147:16", scriptureExplanation: "God's power extends to the weather. Even the cold is under His command — nothing in nature is outside His control." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He casts forth his ice like morsels; who can stand before his cold? — Psalm 147:17", scriptureExplanation: "God's creation is awe-inspiring. Even the cold commands reverence — His power is felt in every season." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He sends out his word and melts them; he makes his wind blow and the waters flow. — Psalm 147:18", scriptureExplanation: "God's word changes the weather. What He freezes, He can thaw — His power is both creative and restorative." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He declares his word to Jacob, his statutes and rules to Israel. — Psalm 147:19", scriptureExplanation: "God reveals Himself through His word. His statutes are a gift — they show us how to live in alignment with His design." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He has not dealt thus with any other nation; they do not know his rules. Praise the Lord! — Psalm 147:20", scriptureExplanation: "God's revelation is a privilege. His word is a gift not everyone has received — and our response should be praise." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise the Lord from the heavens; praise him in the heights! — Psalm 148:1", scriptureExplanation: "Praise begins above. The call to worship starts in the heavens — creation itself is invited to lead." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise him, sun and moon, praise him, all you shining stars! — Psalm 148:3", scriptureExplanation: "The cosmos praises God. The sun, moon, and stars are called to worship — all creation has a voice." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise the Lord from the earth, you great sea creatures and all deeps. — Psalm 148:7", scriptureExplanation: "Praise rises from the depths. Even the sea creatures are invited — worship is not limited to humans." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Kings of the earth and all peoples, princes and all rulers of the earth! — Psalm 148:11", scriptureExplanation: "Everyone is invited to praise. From kings to commoners — worship is the equalizer, the universal calling." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let them praise the name of the Lord, for his name alone is exalted. — Psalm 148:13a", scriptureExplanation: "God's name is above all. His majesty is unique — no other name is worthy of the same exaltation." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise the Lord! Sing to the Lord a new song, his praise in the assembly of the godly! — Psalm 149:1", scriptureExplanation: "New songs reflect new mercies. Each day brings fresh reasons to praise — worship should never grow stale." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let Israel be glad in his Maker; let the children of Zion rejoice in their King! — Psalm 149:2", scriptureExplanation: "Gladness in God is fitting. He is both Maker and King — our Creator and our Ruler, worthy of celebration." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For the Lord takes pleasure in his people; he adorns the humble with salvation. — Psalm 149:4", scriptureExplanation: "God delights in His people. His pleasure is not grudging — He adorns us with salvation, clothing us in His grace." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let the godly exult in glory; let them sing for joy on their beds. — Psalm 149:5", scriptureExplanation: "Joy is private as well as public. Even on our beds — in quiet moments alone — we can sing for joy." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let the high praises of God be in their throats and two-edged swords in their hands. — Psalm 149:6", scriptureExplanation: "Praise and action go together. Worship in the heart and work in the hand — both are part of godly living." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise the Lord! Praise God in his sanctuary; praise him in his mighty heavens! — Psalm 150:1", scriptureExplanation: "Praise is everywhere. In the sanctuary and in the heavens — God is to be praised in every space." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise him for his mighty deeds; praise him according to his excellent greatness. — Psalm 150:2", scriptureExplanation: "Two reasons to praise: what God has done and who God is. Both His acts and His nature deserve worship." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Praise him with trumpet sound; praise him with lute and harp! — Psalm 150:3", scriptureExplanation: "Music serves worship. Instruments are invited — praise is meant to be expressed with creativity and skill." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let everything that has breath praise the Lord! Praise the Lord! — Psalm 150:6", scriptureExplanation: "The final call: all breath, all praise. Every living thing is invited — worship is the purpose of breath itself." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The fear of the Lord is the beginning of knowledge; fools despise wisdom and instruction. — Proverbs 1:7", scriptureExplanation: "Reverence is the foundation of learning. True knowledge starts with awe of God — not with information, but with worship." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Trust in the Lord with all your heart, and do not lean on your own understanding. — Proverbs 3:5", scriptureExplanation: "Trust replaces self-reliance. Our understanding is limited; God's is not. Leaning on Him is safer than leaning on ourselves." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In all your ways acknowledge him, and he will make straight your paths. — Proverbs 3:6", scriptureExplanation: "Acknowledgment brings direction. When we include God in every decision, our path becomes clear — not because we see it all, but because He does." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Honor the Lord with your wealth and with the firstfruits of all your produce. — Proverbs 3:9", scriptureExplanation: "Generosity honors God. Giving first — not last — shows trust. The firstfruits declare that God comes before our needs." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "My son, do not despise the Lord's discipline or be weary of his reproof, for the Lord reproves him whom he loves, as a father the son in whom he delights. — Proverbs 3:11-12", scriptureExplanation: "Discipline is evidence of love. God corrects those He cares about — His reproof is not rejection but investment." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Keep your heart with all vigilance, for from it flow the springs of life. — Proverbs 4:23", scriptureExplanation: "The heart is the source. What we allow into our inner life determines what flows out — guarding the heart is guarding everything." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Trust in the Lord at all times, you people; pour out your heart before him; God is a refuge for us. — Psalm 62:8", scriptureExplanation: "Trust is constant, not occasional. We pour out our hearts — not just our needs — and find God to be our refuge." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He only is my rock and my salvation, my fortress; I shall not be greatly shaken. — Psalm 62:2", scriptureExplanation: "God alone is the foundation. When He is our rock, shaking is minimal — stability comes from singularity of trust." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For God alone, O my soul, wait in silence, for my hope is from him. — Psalm 62:5", scriptureExplanation: "Silent waiting is active trust. David commands his soul to wait — in quietness, hope is renewed." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He only is my rock and my salvation, my fortress; I shall not be shaken. — Psalm 62:6", scriptureExplanation: "Repetition deepens conviction. David says it again — and this time, 'not greatly shaken' becomes 'not shaken.' Faith grows." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "On God rests my salvation and my glory; my mighty rock, my refuge is God. — Psalm 62:7", scriptureExplanation: "Both salvation and glory come from God. Our rescue and our significance are both His gifts — we don't earn either." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Those of low estate are but a breath; those of high estate are a delusion; in the balances they go up; they are together lighter than a breath. — Psalm 62:9", scriptureExplanation: "Human status is weightless. Whether low or high, people can't bear our trust — only God is heavy enough to hold us." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Once God has spoken; twice have I heard this: that power belongs to God. — Psalm 62:11", scriptureExplanation: "God's power is certain. David heard it twice — power is God's alone. No one else has the strength we need." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And that to you, O Lord, belongs steadfast love. For you will render to a man according to his work. — Psalm 62:12", scriptureExplanation: "Power and love both belong to God. He is strong enough to save and loving enough to care — both define Him." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "So teach us to number our days that we may get a heart of wisdom. — Psalm 90:12", scriptureExplanation: "Numbering days brings wisdom. Awareness of life's brevity leads to wise living — not morbidly, but purposefully." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Satisfy us in the morning with your steadfast love, that we may rejoice and be glad all our days. — Psalm 90:14", scriptureExplanation: "Morning satisfaction leads to all-day joy. Starting the day in God's love shapes everything that follows." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Make us glad for as many days as you have afflicted us, and for as many years as we have seen evil. — Psalm 90:15", scriptureExplanation: "God's gladness matches our affliction. The joy He gives is proportional to the pain we've endured — He restores fully." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let your work be shown to your servants, and your glorious power to their children. — Psalm 90:16", scriptureExplanation: "God's work is visible. We ask to see it — and we want our children to see it too. Revelation is generational." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let the favor of the Lord our God be upon us, and establish the work of our hands upon us; yes, establish the work of our hands! — Psalm 90:17", scriptureExplanation: "God's favor establishes our work. Without Him, our efforts are fragile; with Him, they endure. We need His backing." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He who dwells in the shelter of the Most High will abide in the shadow of the Almighty. — Psalm 91:1", scriptureExplanation: "Dwelling brings protection. The one who lives in God's presence finds shelter — not occasional visits, but constant dwelling." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I will say to the Lord, 'My refuge and my fortress, my God, in whom I trust.' — Psalm 91:2", scriptureExplanation: "Declaration strengthens trust. Saying it out loud — 'my refuge, my fortress' — reinforces what we believe." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He will cover you with his pinions, and under his wings you will find refuge; his faithfulness is a shield and buckler. — Psalm 91:4", scriptureExplanation: "God's protection is intimate — like a bird covering its young. His faithfulness is both shield (large) and buckler (small, close)." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You will not fear the terror of the night, nor the arrow that flies by day. — Psalm 91:5", scriptureExplanation: "Fear is removed by trust. Both nighttime terrors and daytime threats lose their power when we're under God's protection." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "A thousand may fall at your side, ten thousand at your right hand, but it will not come near you. — Psalm 91:7", scriptureExplanation: "God's protection is specific. Even in widespread destruction, His care is personal — it won't come near you." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Because you have made the Lord your dwelling place, the Most High, who is my refuge. — Psalm 91:9", scriptureExplanation: "Dwelling is the condition. Making God our home — not just a shelter — brings the fullness of His protection." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For he will command his angels concerning you to guard you in all your ways. — Psalm 91:11", scriptureExplanation: "God commands angels on our behalf. His protection includes unseen servants — angelic guards assigned by His word." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "On their hands they will bear you up, lest you strike your foot against a stone. — Psalm 91:12", scriptureExplanation: "God's care is detailed. Even a stubbed toe is noticed — His protection extends to the smallest dangers." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "When he calls to me, I will answer him; I will be with him in trouble; I will rescue him and honor him. — Psalm 91:15", scriptureExplanation: "God answers, accompanies, rescues, and honors. Four promises — each one personal, each one powerful." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "With long life I will satisfy him and show him my salvation. — Psalm 91:16", scriptureExplanation: "Satisfaction and salvation are God's gifts. Long life is not just duration but fulfillment — and it ends in seeing His salvation." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "It is good to give thanks to the Lord, to sing praises to your name, O Most High. — Psalm 92:1", scriptureExplanation: "Gratitude is good. Giving thanks is not just polite — it's the right response to God's goodness." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "To declare your steadfast love in the morning, and your faithfulness by night. — Psalm 92:2", scriptureExplanation: "God's love and faithfulness frame the day. Morning and night — we begin and end with His character." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For you, O Lord, have made me glad by your work; at the works of your hands I sing for joy. — Psalm 92:4", scriptureExplanation: "God's work brings joy. What He has done is a reason to sing — His creation and His providence both inspire worship." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "How great are your works, O Lord! Your thoughts are very deep! — Psalm 92:5", scriptureExplanation: "God's works are great and His thoughts are deep. We can see the surface but not the depths — His wisdom surpasses ours." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The stupid man cannot know; the fool cannot understand this: that though the wicked sprout like grass and all evildoers flourish, they will be destroyed forever. — Psalm 92:6-7", scriptureExplanation: "Appearances deceive. Temporary flourishing is not permanent success — God's justice will have the final word." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But you, O Lord, are on high forever. — Psalm 92:8", scriptureExplanation: "God's position is permanent. He is above all, always — His sovereignty never changes, regardless of circumstances." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For behold, your enemies, O Lord, for behold, your enemies shall perish; all evildoers shall be scattered. — Psalm 92:9", scriptureExplanation: "Evil has an expiration date. God will scatter evildoers — injustice is temporary, His justice is eternal." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But you have exalted my horn like that of the wild ox; you have poured over me fresh oil. — Psalm 92:10", scriptureExplanation: "God strengthens and anoints. The horn represents power; the oil represents consecration — both are His gifts." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "My eyes have seen the downfall of my enemies; my ears have heard the doom of my evil foes. — Psalm 92:11", scriptureExplanation: "God's vindication is visible. David witnesses God's justice — not just believes in it, but sees it." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The righteous flourish like the palm tree and grow like a cedar in Lebanon. — Psalm 92:12", scriptureExplanation: "Righteousness leads to flourishing. The palm and cedar are both strong and enduring — the righteous grow, not just survive." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "They are planted in the house of the Lord; they flourish in the courts of our God. — Psalm 92:13", scriptureExplanation: "Location determines flourishing. Planted in God's house — rooted in His presence — growth is natural and sustained." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "They still bear fruit in old age; they are ever full of sap and green. — Psalm 92:14", scriptureExplanation: "Fruitfulness has no age limit. Even in old age, the righteous are vibrant — full of life, still producing." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "To declare that the Lord is upright; he is my rock, and there is no unrighteousness in him. — Psalm 92:15", scriptureExplanation: "God's character is flawless. He is rock-solid and perfectly just — declaring this is the purpose of flourishing." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Lord, you have been our dwelling place in all generations. — Psalm 90:1", scriptureExplanation: "God is home. Not a temporary shelter but a dwelling place — and not just for us, but for every generation." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever you had formed the earth and the world, from everlasting to everlasting you are God. — Psalm 90:2", scriptureExplanation: "God is eternal. Before creation, He was. From everlasting to everlasting — His existence has no beginning or end." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You return man to dust and say, 'Return, O children of man!' — Psalm 90:3", scriptureExplanation: "God is sovereign over life and death. He calls us back to dust — a reminder of our frailty and His authority." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For a thousand years in your sight are but as yesterday when it is past, or as a watch in the night. — Psalm 90:4", scriptureExplanation: "God's time is different. A millennium is like a day to Him — our urgency is met by His eternity." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You sweep them away as with a flood; they are like a dream, like grass that is renewed in the morning. — Psalm 90:5", scriptureExplanation: "Life is fleeting. Like a dream or morning grass — beautiful but brief. This is not despair, but perspective." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In the morning it flourishes and is renewed; in the evening it fades and withers. — Psalm 90:6", scriptureExplanation: "Human life has a rhythm. Morning flourishing, evening fading — we are seasonal, but God is constant." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For we are brought to an end by your anger; by your wrath we are dismayed. — Psalm 90:7", scriptureExplanation: "Sin has consequences. God's anger is real — and our frailty is partly a result of our brokenness before Him." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "You have set our iniquities before you, our secret sins in the light of your presence. — Psalm 90:8", scriptureExplanation: "Nothing is hidden from God. Our secret sins are exposed in His light — honesty before Him is the only path forward." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For all our days pass away under your wrath; we bring our years to an end like a sigh. — Psalm 90:9", scriptureExplanation: "Life without God is empty. Years end like a sigh — but this is the problem, not the plan. God offers more." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The years of our life are seventy, or even by reason of strength eighty; yet their span is but toil and trouble; they are soon gone, and we fly away. — Psalm 90:10", scriptureExplanation: "Life is short and hard. But the recognition of brevity is meant to drive us to God, not to despair." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Who considers the power of your anger, and your wrath according to the fear of you? — Psalm 90:11", scriptureExplanation: "Few grasp the weight of God's holiness. Reverence is not popular but it's necessary — it's the beginning of wisdom." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Return, O Lord! How long? Have pity on your servants! — Psalm 90:13", scriptureExplanation: "Moses cries out for God's return. The question 'how long?' is honest — and the plea for pity is bold." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let your work be shown to your servants, and your glorious power to their children. — Psalm 90:16", scriptureExplanation: "Moses asks for visible works. Not just for us but for our children — God's power is meant to be seen across generations." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And let the favor of the Lord our God be upon us, and establish the work of our hands upon us. — Psalm 90:17a", scriptureExplanation: "God's favor makes our work last. Without it, we build in vain; with it, our efforts are established — meaning is restored." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Bless the Lord, O my soul, and all that is within me, bless his holy name! — Psalm 103:1", scriptureExplanation: "David commands his whole being to worship. 'All that is within me' — nothing held back, everything engaged in praise." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Bless the Lord, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits. — Psalm 103:2", scriptureExplanation: "Forgetfulness kills gratitude. David warns his soul not to forget — remembering God's benefits is the fuel of worship." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Who forgives all your iniquity, who heals all your diseases. — Psalm 103:3", scriptureExplanation: "God's forgiveness and healing are both comprehensive. 'All' — not some, not most, but all. His grace is total." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Who redeems your life from the pit, who crowns you with steadfast love and mercy. — Psalm 103:4", scriptureExplanation: "God rescues and crowns. He lifts us from the pit and then places a crown on our head — redemption leads to dignity." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Who satisfies you with good so that your youth is renewed like the eagle's. — Psalm 103:5", scriptureExplanation: "God's satisfaction brings renewal. Like an eagle molting and regaining strength — His goodness makes us young again." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord works righteousness and justice for all who are oppressed. — Psalm 103:6", scriptureExplanation: "God's justice is active. He works on behalf of the oppressed — His righteousness is not theoretical but practical." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He made known his ways to Moses, his acts to the people of Israel. — Psalm 103:7", scriptureExplanation: "God reveals Himself. His ways to Moses, His acts to the people — He makes Himself known, both in principle and in power." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord is merciful and gracious, slow to anger and abounding in steadfast love. — Psalm 103:8", scriptureExplanation: "God's character is mercy. He is slow to anger and full of love — this is who He is, not just what He does." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He will not always chide, nor will he keep his anger forever. — Psalm 103:9", scriptureExplanation: "God's anger is temporary. He doesn't hold grudges — His discipline has an end, but His love does not." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He does not deal with us according to our sins, nor repay us according to our iniquities. — Psalm 103:10", scriptureExplanation: "God doesn't give us what we deserve. His treatment is based on mercy, not merit — grace redefines our account." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For as high as the heavens are above the earth, so great is his steadfast love toward those who fear him. — Psalm 103:11", scriptureExplanation: "God's love is immeasurable. As high as the heavens — that's how vast His love is for those who revere Him." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "As far as the east is from the west, so far does he remove our transgressions from us. — Psalm 103:12", scriptureExplanation: "God's forgiveness is total. East and west never meet — that's how completely He separates us from our sins." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "As a father shows compassion to his children, so the Lord shows compassion to those who fear him. — Psalm 103:13", scriptureExplanation: "God's compassion is fatherly. He treats us like a loving parent — with tenderness, patience, and deep affection." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For he knows our frame; he remembers that we are dust. — Psalm 103:14", scriptureExplanation: "God understands our weakness. He knows we're made of dust — His expectations are shaped by His understanding." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "As for man, his days are like grass; he flourishes like a flower of the field. — Psalm 103:15", scriptureExplanation: "Human life is beautiful but brief. Like a wildflower — vivid today, gone tomorrow. This is not a complaint but a call to dependence." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For the wind passes over it, and it is gone, and its place knows it no more. — Psalm 103:16", scriptureExplanation: "Impermanence is real. But God's love is not impermanent — He outlasts the wind and the flower." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But the steadfast love of the Lord is from everlasting to everlasting on those who fear him. — Psalm 103:17a", scriptureExplanation: "God's love is eternal. From everlasting to everlasting — it preceded our existence and will outlast our days." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And his righteousness to children's children, to those who keep his covenant and remember to do his commandments. — Psalm 103:17b-18", scriptureExplanation: "God's righteousness is generational. His faithfulness extends to our children's children — covenant living has a legacy." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The Lord has established his throne in the heavens, and his kingdom rules over all. — Psalm 103:19", scriptureExplanation: "God's rule is universal. His throne is in heaven, His kingdom over all — nothing is outside His sovereignty." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Bless the Lord, all his angels, mighty in strength, who do his word, obeying the voice of his word! — Psalm 103:20", scriptureExplanation: "Even angels worship. The strongest beings in creation bless God — power is meant to serve praise." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Bless the Lord, all his hosts, his ministers, who do his will! — Psalm 103:21", scriptureExplanation: "All of heaven serves and worships. God's ministers do His will and bless His name — the whole universe is a choir." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Bless the Lord, O my soul! — Psalm 103:22", scriptureExplanation: "David ends where he began. The soul that started praising must keep praising — worship is a circle, not a line." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Let all that I am praise the Lord; I will praise the Lord as long as I live. — Psalm 146:1-2a (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Total, lifelong praise. Every part of who I am, for as long as I am — worship is whole-life and whole-life-long." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Do not be anxious about anything, but in everything by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known to God. — Philippians 4:6", scriptureExplanation: "Anxiety is replaced by prayer. Not worry → peace, but worry → prayer → peace. Thanksgiving is the bridge." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "If God is for us, who can be against us? — Romans 8:31b", scriptureExplanation: "God's support is decisive. If He is for us, opposition is irrelevant — His presence tips every scale." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "He who did not spare his own Son but gave him up for us all, how will he not also with him graciously give us all things? — Romans 8:32", scriptureExplanation: "God's greatest gift guarantees the rest. If He gave us Jesus, He'll give us everything else we need — the logic of grace." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Who shall bring any charge against God's elect? It is God who justifies. — Romans 8:33", scriptureExplanation: "God's verdict is final. If He declares us right, no accusation sticks — His justification is the ultimate defense." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Who is to condemn? Christ Jesus is the one who died — more than that, who was raised — who is at the right hand of God, who indeed is interceding for us. — Romans 8:34", scriptureExplanation: "No condemnation remains. Jesus died, rose, and now prays for us — His intercession is ongoing and effective." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Who shall separate us from the love of Christ? Shall tribulation, or distress, or persecution, or famine, or nakedness, or danger, or sword? — Romans 8:35", scriptureExplanation: "Nothing can break God's love. Paul lists every possible threat — and none of them can sever us from Christ's love." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "No, in all these things we are more than conquerors through him who loved us. — Romans 8:37", scriptureExplanation: "We don't just survive — we conquer. And not just conquer, but 'more than' conquer. Love makes us overwhelming victors." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For I am sure that neither death nor life, nor angels nor rulers, nor things present nor things to come, nor powers, nor height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God in Christ Jesus our Lord. — Romans 8:38-39", scriptureExplanation: "Paul's absolute certainty. Every possible separator is named and dismissed — God's love is inseparable, unbreakable, eternal." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "I have been crucified with Christ. It is no longer I who live, but Christ who lives in me. And the life I now live in the flesh I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave himself for me. — Galatians 2:20", scriptureExplanation: "Identity is redefined. The old self is dead; Christ now lives within. Faith is the new mode of existence — daily reliance on His love." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For freedom Christ has set us free; stand firm therefore, and do not submit again to a yoke of slavery. — Galatians 5:1", scriptureExplanation: "Freedom is both gift and responsibility. Christ freed us — now we must stand firm and not slip back into old bondage." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For you were called to freedom, brothers. Only do not use your freedom as an opportunity for the flesh, but through love serve one another. — Galatians 5:13", scriptureExplanation: "Freedom is for love, not license. We're free so we can serve — liberty is redirected toward others, not indulgence." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But I say, walk by the Spirit, and you will not gratify the desires of the flesh. — Galatians 5:16", scriptureExplanation: "Spirit-led living prevents sin. Walking by the Spirit is the alternative to fleshly desire — not willpower, but a different direction." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "If we live by the Spirit, let us also keep in step with the Spirit. — Galatians 5:25", scriptureExplanation: "Life in the Spirit requires alignment. Living by the Spirit and walking with the Spirit are connected — both are necessary." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And let us not grow weary of doing good, for in due season we will reap, if we do not give up. — Galatians 6:9", scriptureExplanation: "Doing good is tiring but fruitful. The harvest is coming — but only if we persist. Weariness is normal; quitting is the only failure." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "So then, as we have opportunity, let us do good to everyone, and especially to those who are of the household of faith. — Galatians 6:10", scriptureExplanation: "Good is to be done to all, with priority to family. Opportunity is the guide — we do good when and where we can." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But far be it from me to boast except in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, by which the world has been crucified to me, and I to the world. — Galatians 6:14", scriptureExplanation: "The cross is the only boast. Paul's pride is in what Christ did, not what he achieved — the cross redefines glory." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For neither circumcision counts for anything, nor uncircumcision, but a new creation. — Galatians 6:15", scriptureExplanation: "External marks don't matter — transformation does. What counts is being made new, not fitting a religious category." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And as for all who walk by this rule, peace and mercy be upon them, and upon the Israel of God. — Galatians 6:16", scriptureExplanation: "Peace and mercy follow the new creation rule. Walking in transformation brings blessing — the rule of Christ leads to peace." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "From now on let no one cause me trouble, for I bear on my body the marks of Jesus. — Galatians 6:17", scriptureExplanation: "Paul's scars are his credentials. The marks of suffering for Christ are proof of authenticity — hardship is not a disqualification." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit, brothers. Amen. — Galatians 6:18", scriptureExplanation: "Grace is personal. Paul's final blessing is for their spirit — grace reaches the deepest part of who we are." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us in Christ with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly places. — Ephesians 1:3", scriptureExplanation: "Every spiritual blessing is already ours. Not some, not future — every blessing, given now, in Christ." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Even as he chose us in him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and blameless before him. — Ephesians 1:4", scriptureExplanation: "God's choice preceded creation. He chose us before the world began — our identity was established in eternity." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In love he predestined us for adoption to himself as sons through Jesus Christ, according to the purpose of his will. — Ephesians 1:5", scriptureExplanation: "Adoption is the goal. God didn't just save us — He adopted us. Love drove the choice; family is the result." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "To the praise of his glorious grace, with which he has blessed us in the Beloved. — Ephesians 1:6", scriptureExplanation: "Grace leads to praise. God's blessing is not just for our benefit — it's designed to display His glory." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In him we have redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of our trespasses, according to the riches of his grace. — Ephesians 1:7", scriptureExplanation: "Redemption is through Christ's blood. Forgiveness is not cheap — it cost everything. Grace is free but not gratuitous." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Which he lavished upon us, in all wisdom and insight. — Ephesians 1:8", scriptureExplanation: "God's grace is lavish. Not measured, not stingy — poured out in abundance, with wisdom behind every drop." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Making known to us the mystery of his will, according to his purpose, which he set forth in Christ. — Ephesians 1:9", scriptureExplanation: "God reveals His plan. The mystery of His will is made known — not hidden, but disclosed, in Christ." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "As a plan for the fullness of time, to unite all things in him, things in heaven and things on earth. — Ephesians 1:10", scriptureExplanation: "God's plan is unification. All things — heaven and earth — brought together in Christ. The end is unity, not fragmentation." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In him we have obtained an inheritance, having been predestined according to the purpose of him who works all things according to the counsel of his will. — Ephesians 1:11", scriptureExplanation: "Our inheritance is certain. God works all things according to His will — our future is secured by His sovereignty." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "So that we who were the first to hope in Christ might be to the praise of his glory. — Ephesians 1:12", scriptureExplanation: "Hope leads to praise. Our hope in Christ has a purpose — to display God's glory. We are living evidence of His grace." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In him you also, when you heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation, and believed in him, were sealed with the promised Holy Spirit. — Ephesians 1:13", scriptureExplanation: "The Spirit is our seal. Belief in the gospel brings the Spirit — He marks us as God's own, a guarantee of what's to come." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Who is the guarantee of our inheritance until we acquire possession of it, to the praise of his glory. — Ephesians 1:14", scriptureExplanation: "The Spirit is a down payment. He guarantees our future — the full inheritance is coming, and the Spirit is the earnest." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For this reason, because I have heard of your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love toward all the saints, I do not cease to give thanks for you, remembering you in my prayers. — Ephesians 1:15-16", scriptureExplanation: "Paul prays with gratitude. Faith and love prompt thanksgiving — and prayer for others is a form of love." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "That the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give you the Spirit of wisdom and of revelation in the knowledge of him. — Ephesians 1:17", scriptureExplanation: "Knowing God requires revelation. Wisdom and revelation are gifts — we can't know God by intellect alone; He must disclose Himself." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Having the eyes of your hearts enlightened, that you may know what is the hope to which he has called you. — Ephesians 1:18a", scriptureExplanation: "Heart-knowledge is deeper than head-knowledge. Enlightened eyes of the heart see hope — true understanding is spiritual, not just intellectual." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "What are the riches of his glorious inheritance in the saints. — Ephesians 1:18b", scriptureExplanation: "Our inheritance is glorious. The riches are not just for us — they are in us, among God's people, shared and communal." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And what is the immeasurable greatness of his power toward us who believe, according to the working of his great might. — Ephesians 1:19", scriptureExplanation: "God's power is for us. Not just in the universe — toward us who believe. The same power that raised Christ works in our lives." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "That he worked in Christ when he raised him from the dead and seated him at his right hand in the heavenly places. — Ephesians 1:20", scriptureExplanation: "Resurrection power is ours. The power that raised and seated Christ is the power at work in us — immeasurable, unstoppable." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Far above all rule and authority and power and dominion, and above every name that is named, not only in this age but also in the one to come. — Ephesians 1:21", scriptureExplanation: "Christ is above all. Every power, every name, every authority — Christ surpasses them all, now and forever." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And he put all things under his feet and gave him as head over all things to the church. — Ephesians 1:22", scriptureExplanation: "Christ's headship is for the church. All things are under His feet — and He is given to us as head. Authority and intimacy together." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Which is his body, the fullness of him who fills all in all. — Ephesians 1:23", scriptureExplanation: "The church is Christ's fullness. He fills all in all — and we are His body. The image is staggering: we are the completion of His presence on earth." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But God, being rich in mercy, because of the great love with which he loved us, even when we were dead in our trespasses, made us alive together with Christ — by grace you have been saved. — Ephesians 2:4-5", scriptureExplanation: "God acted when we were dead. Not when we were trying — when we were dead. His love and mercy moved first; grace precedes response." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And raised us up with him and seated us with him in the heavenly places in Christ Jesus. — Ephesians 2:6", scriptureExplanation: "Our position is in heaven. We are already seated with Christ — not just promised a future, but given a present reality." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "So that in the coming ages he might show the immeasurable riches of his grace in kindness toward us in Christ Jesus. — Ephesians 2:7", scriptureExplanation: "God's grace is on eternal display. The coming ages will showcase His kindness — we are the exhibit of His grace." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For by grace you have been saved through faith. And this is not your own doing; it is the gift of God. — Ephesians 2:8", scriptureExplanation: "Salvation is a gift. Not earned, not merited — received. Grace excludes boasting and includes everyone who believes." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Not a result of works, so that no one may boast. — Ephesians 2:9", scriptureExplanation: "Works are excluded from salvation. Not because they don't matter, but because they can't save — only grace can." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God prepared beforehand, that we should walk in them. — Ephesians 2:10", scriptureExplanation: "We are God's artwork. Created for good works — not saved by them, but saved for them. Our deeds were prepared in advance." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Therefore remember that at one time you Gentiles in the flesh, called 'the uncircumcision' by what is called the circumcision, which is made in the flesh by hands. — Ephesians 2:11", scriptureExplanation: "Remember the past. Paul calls Gentiles to recall what they were — memory of separation makes the unity sweeter." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Remember that you were at that time separated from Christ, alienated from the commonwealth of Israel and strangers to the covenants of promise, having no hope and without God in the world. — Ephesians 2:12", scriptureExplanation: "Without Christ, without hope. Paul describes the pre-Christian state starkly — no hope, no God. The contrast makes grace shine." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "But now in Christ Jesus you who once were far off have been brought near by the blood of Christ. — Ephesians 2:13", scriptureExplanation: "Christ's blood brings near. The distance is closed — not by our approach, but by His sacrifice. Nearness is His gift." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For he himself is our peace, who has made us both one and has broken down in his flesh the dividing wall of hostility. — Ephesians 2:14", scriptureExplanation: "Christ is our peace. Not just a peacemaker — He IS peace. The wall of hostility is broken in His body." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "By abolishing the law of commandments expressed in ordinances, that he might create in himself one new man in place of the two, so making peace. — Ephesians 2:15", scriptureExplanation: "Christ creates one new humanity. The division is replaced by unity — a new identity that transcends old categories." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And might reconcile us both to God in one body through the cross, thereby killing the hostility. — Ephesians 2:16", scriptureExplanation: "Reconciliation is through the cross. The cross kills hostility — between people and between us and God. One act, two reconciliations." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And he came and preached peace to you who were far off and peace to those who were near. — Ephesians 2:17", scriptureExplanation: "Christ preaches peace to all. Far and near — the message is the same. Peace is for everyone, through Him." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For through him we both have access in one Spirit to the Father. — Ephesians 2:18", scriptureExplanation: "Access to the Father is through Christ. The Spirit brings us in — the whole Trinity is involved in our approach to God." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "So then you are no longer strangers and aliens, but you are fellow citizens with the saints and members of the household of God. — Ephesians 2:19", scriptureExplanation: "Belonging is redefined. No longer outsiders — now family. Citizenship and household membership are both given." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, Christ Jesus himself being the cornerstone. — Ephesians 2:20", scriptureExplanation: "Christ is the cornerstone. The foundation is apostolic and prophetic — but the cornerstone, the alignment point, is Jesus Himself." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In whom the whole structure, being joined together, grows into a holy temple in the Lord. — Ephesians 2:21", scriptureExplanation: "We grow together into a temple. Not isolated stones — a joined structure. Growth is communal, not just individual." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In him you also are being built together into a dwelling place for God by the Spirit. — Ephesians 2:22", scriptureExplanation: "We are God's dwelling. The Spirit builds us together — we become the place where God lives. The temple is now people." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For this reason I, Paul, a prisoner for Christ Jesus on behalf of you Gentiles. — Ephesians 3:1", scriptureExplanation: "Paul's imprisonment is for others. His suffering is purposeful — it's for the Gentiles. Chains have meaning when they're for Christ." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Assuming that you have heard of the stewardship of God's grace that was given to me for you. — Ephesians 3:2", scriptureExplanation: "Grace has a stewardship. Paul received grace to give it away — it's not just for him but for others. Grace is meant to flow." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "How the mystery was made known to me by revelation, as I have written briefly. — Ephesians 3:3", scriptureExplanation: "Revelation, not research. Paul received the mystery — he didn't discover it. God disclosed what human effort couldn't find." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "When you read this, you can perceive my insight into the mystery of Christ. — Ephesians 3:4", scriptureExplanation: "Revelation is communicable. Paul's insight can be perceived by readers — the mystery is not private but shareable." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Which was not made known to the sons of men in other generations as it has now been revealed to his holy apostles and prophets by the Spirit. — Ephesians 3:5", scriptureExplanation: "The mystery is now revealed. What was hidden is now disclosed — the Spirit reveals to the apostles what previous generations couldn't see." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "This mystery is that the Gentiles are fellow heirs, members of the same body, and partakers of the promise in Christ Jesus through the gospel. — Ephesians 3:6", scriptureExplanation: "The mystery is inclusion. Gentiles are heirs, members, and partakers — the gospel breaks every barrier. Unity is the mystery revealed." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Of this gospel I was made a minister according to the gift of God's grace, which was given me by the working of his power. — Ephesians 3:7", scriptureExplanation: "Ministry is a grace gift. Paul didn't earn it — God gave it. Service flows from grace, not from qualification." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "To me, though I am the very least of all the saints, this grace was given, to preach to the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ. — Ephesians 3:8", scriptureExplanation: "Paul's humility is genuine. The least of all saints — yet given the greatest task. Grace doesn't require greatness; it creates it." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And to bring to light for everyone what is the plan of the mystery hidden for ages in God who created all things. — Ephesians 3:9", scriptureExplanation: "The mystery is for everyone. Not just for the elite — for all. God's plan, hidden for ages, is now brought into the light." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "So that through the church the manifold wisdom of God might now be made known to the rulers and authorities in the heavenly places. — Ephesians 3:10", scriptureExplanation: "The church displays God's wisdom. Even cosmic powers learn from us — the church is God's object lesson to the universe." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "This was according to the eternal purpose that he has realized in Christ Jesus our Lord. — Ephesians 3:11", scriptureExplanation: "God's plan is eternal. It was always the purpose — realized in Christ. The church is not a backup plan; it's the original design." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "In whom we have boldness and access with confidence through our faith in him. — Ephesians 3:12", scriptureExplanation: "Faith brings boldness. Access to God is confident, not timid — we approach through faith, not fear." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "So I ask you not to lose heart over what I am suffering for you, which is your glory. — Ephesians 3:13", scriptureExplanation: "Suffering has purpose. Paul's imprisonment is for their glory — hardship for others is not wasted but redemptive." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "For this reason I bow my knees before the Father, from whom every family in heaven and on earth is named. — Ephesians 3:14-15", scriptureExplanation: "Paul prays on his knees. Every family derives from God — He is the source of all belonging. Prayer acknowledges this." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "That according to the riches of his glory he may grant you to be strengthened with power through his Spirit in your inner being. — Ephesians 3:16", scriptureExplanation: "Inner strength comes from the Spirit. Not outer willpower — inner power. The Spirit strengthens us at the deepest level." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "So that Christ may dwell in your hearts through faith — that you, being rooted and grounded in love. — Ephesians 3:17", scriptureExplanation: "Christ dwells in the heart by faith. Rooted and grounded in love — like a tree and a building, stable because of love." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "May have strength to comprehend with all the saints what is the breadth and length and height and depth. — Ephesians 3:18", scriptureExplanation: "God's love has dimensions. Breadth, length, height, depth — it's measurable only in community, with all the saints." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "And to know the love of Christ that surpasses knowledge, that you may be filled with all the fullness of God. — Ephesians 3:19", scriptureExplanation: "Knowing what surpasses knowledge. Christ's love is beyond understanding — yet we can know it, and be filled with God's fullness." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "Now to him who is able to do far more abundantly than all that we ask or think, according to the power at work within us. — Ephesians 3:20", scriptureExplanation: "God exceeds our imagination. More than we ask or think — His power within us is greater than our wildest prayers." },
  { category: "christian", scripture: "To him be glory in the church and in Christ Jesus throughout all generations, forever and ever. Amen. — Ephesians 3:21", scriptureExplanation: "Glory is eternal and generational. In the church, in Christ, across all generations — God's glory is unending." },
];